  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation for rural livelihoods in Zimbabwe Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to reduce rural livelihoods&apos; vulnerability to climate change through enhancing and scaling up food -climate -natural resources -biodiversity nexus adaptation measures that ensure sustainable household food, income, and nutrition security. The project vision is that of a resilient Zimbabwe, where rural communities and institutions are better able to anticipate, adapt, and respond to climate shocks and other stresses, and take charge of their own inclusive development, and achieve food and nutrition security while sustainably managing diverse natural resources and biodiversity.</narrative>
  </description>
